      "message": "Can this binding use different behavior from the default around I2C? It\u0027s not clear here that this refers to the port TCPC unless `USB_MUX_FLAG_NOT_TCPC` is set: perhaps make them mutually required so it\u0027s an error to specify I2C information unless `NOT_TCPC` is specified (and if it is, then I2C information is required)? Or even infer `NOT_TCPC` based on I2C information and document that behavior in this binding.\n\nHaving this hold a reference to the TCPC would be nice since there wouldn\u0027t be a magic mapping through the port, but that doesn\u0027t seem possible at the moment since the TCPC doesn\u0027t currently appear in the device tree.",
